    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "150f4084_81b671ac",
        "filename": "packages/Tethering/src/com/android/server/connectivity/tethering/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 1129,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-16T13:26:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If USB is already in use with some other function it seems to me we may want to keep them activated (maybe we can\u0027t have regular USB tethering at the same time as NCM tethering, but maybe MTP can be active at the same time for example). Should we just logical-or NCM to the currently set functions rather than resetting everything, killing other current functions ?\n\nOr, is there a reason this would not work ? If so, is there any way to warn the user the other functions are getting deactivated ?\n\n\nNote that it\u0027s relevant when enable \u003d true, but it\u0027s even more relevant when enable \u003d false. If for some reason NCM tethering is not active, but there is a call to this with enable \u003d false, all other USB functions get deactivated and I don\u0027t think that\u0027s expected.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1129,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 1129,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "b745b96544cfd169fe10780e6ab4b5a2c4fd3def",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
